{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-142395","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"boycott animal-tested products\" \"boycott products tested on animals\" \"purchase cruelty free products\") (+ students teens teenagers))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"boycott animal-tested products\" \"boycott products tested on animals\" \"purchase cruelty free products\") (+ students teens teenagers))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#0_1416301827","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1015","rank":1,"snippet":": \"The darker side of cosmetic testing - nj.com The darker side of cosmetic testing Updated Mar 31, 2019; Posted Mar 13, 2011 By Cranford Chronicle By Olivia Dineen When you put on your makeup in the morning, do you ever think about the millions of animals that have been killed to test the product? Many name-brand companies such as L'Oreal, Johnson and Johnson, and Dial Corporation use animals to test their products for safety. Consumers should boycott animal-tested products and only <cover>purchase cruelty free products. It is time for us to make this issue known and to save the rabbits, cats, dogs, and primates that need our help. Students </cover>grapple with key issues Each year, teacher Lore Walsh's eighth grade students at Hillside Avenue School in Cranford write persuasive articles as part of a problem solving unit. They learn about voice, audience, credibility and different types of appeal. To make the experience more meaningful, the students are asked to publish their final pieces. They may send them to a specific person, display them on a school bulletin board, or send them to the newspaper. The harsh tests performed on animals in labs are very ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#0_1416301827","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":395},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":21,"relevance_3":1,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-142395","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1015"},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":21,"relevance_3":1,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-142395","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1015"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1015"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#5_1416309427","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1015","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#5_1416309427\" , \"end_char\": 3659.000000 , \"headings\": \"The darker side of cosmetic testing The darker side of cosmetic testing<cover>Students grapple with key issues Around the web \" , \"segment\": \"Plenty of organizations, such as PETA, have lists of companies that do and don’t test on animals. If you boycott animal tested products, </cover>these companies will be forced to change the way they test. Finally, there is an enormous cost to testing on animals. Do you really want your tax dollars going to labs to perform tests that sometimes don’t even work? Labs need money to do research on the testing and keep the animals (food and shelter). It is practically like paying for animals to be killed. Seems pretty pointless, right? Every day, many animals are harmed or killed in labs all across the country, just so we can have what we want. I’m not saying that products shouldn’t be tested; they should just be tested in a way that is less harmful to animals.\" ,","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#0_1416301827","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":6},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":21,"relevance_3":1,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
