{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-142395","model_call":46,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1026"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1026"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_884204827#0_1799499220","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1026","rank":3,"snippet":"donation. 5. Leave your body to science. 6. Share this page! Follow Us \" , \"segment\": \"6 Ways to Help Animals in Experiments | Action | PETA.org 6 Ways to Help Animals Suffering in Experiments Why are millions of animals STILL suffering in laboratories? There’s no justifiable reason. Companies do not need to torture animals in order to test mascara, shampoo, detergent, or other household products. Scientists do not have to torment monkeys in order to cure a disease. Educators do not need to buy fetal pigs to teach <cover>students physiology. There are easy ways to lend your voice to animals suffering in experiments, and together we can stop animal testing. Here are six ways you can help them (and if you haven’t already, join PETA’s Action Team to help even more animals!). 1. Always buy cruelty-free </cover>products. Cruelty-free cosmetics and household products abound.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"6 Ways to Help Animals in Experiments | Action | PETA.org\" , \"url\": \"https://www.peta.org/action/easy-ways-help-animals-used-killed-experiments/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_348846183#6_766498618","rank":2,"relevance":2}]},"time":10},"model_calls":46,"document_judgments":29,"relevance_3":2,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
